.TH DRAGONGL-CLIENT 1 "2026-10-27" "DragonGL+ 2026.10" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dragongl-client \- Dragon GL client launcher script
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dragongl-client
.RI "[\-\-help\ |\ -h ]"
.RI "[ gl | vk ]"
.RI "[ server_ip ]"
.RI "[ port ]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dragongl-client
is a convenience launcher for the Dragon GL client. It runs
.B build/dragongl_client
when started from a source tree, otherwise the installed
.BR dragongl_client ,
passing every argument unchanged. With no argument the game opens on its
title menu (Play Solo / Join a Server).
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B gl
OpenGL 3.3 renderer (default).
.TP
.B vk
Vulkan 1.3 renderer (falls back to OpenGL if unavailable).
.TP
.I server_ip
(optional) Pre-fill the "Join a Server" form.
.TP
.I port
(optional) Server TCP port (default 8080).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h , \-\-help
Show a short help message and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the client with the Vulkan backend:
.PP
.RS
.B dragongl-client vk
.RE
.PP
Connect directly to a remote server (skips the IP prompt):
.PP
.RS
.B dragongl-client vk 192.168.1.10 9000
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dragongl_client (1),
.BR dragongl-server (1)
